        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: The Last Voyage of Somebody the Sailor; Sinbad the Sailor\n- People/Characters: Sinbad the Sailor; Scheherazade\n- Places: Baghdad; Baghdad, the City of Peace\n- Concepts: Abbasid Caliphate; Middle Eastern story-cycle\n\nFacts:\n- In The Last Voyage of Somebody the Sailor, a character eventually reaches Baghdad, called the City of Peace, and finds himself inside the stories of Sinbad and Scheherazade.\n- Sinbad the Sailor, also spelled Sindbad, is a fictional sailor and the hero of a Middle Eastern story-cycle.\n- Sinbad the Sailor is described as living in Baghdad during the Abbasid Caliphate.\n- The Arabic name of Sinbad the Sailor is ٱلسِّنْدِبَادُ ٱلْبَحرِيّ‎, transliterated as as-Sindibādu al-Baḥriyy.",
